# probe reads x (10), calls poke, which writes the root's x through node, and reads x again: probe answers 10 * 1000 + 10 (the source of x is a row of the
# caller's frame; node\x writes the cell of the graph, not that row). An ordinary row by the norm (the author 2026-11-18: a free name is resolved at its first read
# and held): it does NOT witness the hold -- it passes without any take in the readers; the hold gets a witness with an executable lexical source.
# наблюдение явной записью: локалы не публикуются (#flush-receiver-contract)
(
    Observed:
        int: r 0
)
@: shared data[0]
int: x 10
sub: poke ()
    node\x := 99
fn: probe () int
    int: first x
    poke()
    int: second x
    return: first * 1000 + second
int: r probe()

sub: main ()
    shared\Observed\r := r
main()
